1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,218
What's today's video about? We're picking up trending topics from the latest news!

2
00:00:09,218 --> 00:00:10,718
Scene 1: Free Guided Tours – Explore for Free!

3
00:00:10,718 --> 00:00:13,931
Did you catch the morning news?

4
00:00:13,955 --> 00:00:17,404
No, I didn’t.

5
00:00:17,427 --> 00:00:20,660
It’s about free guided tours!

6
00:00:20,683 --> 00:00:23,617
Free guided tours?

7
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:26,106
What kind of tours?

8
00:00:26,129 --> 00:00:30,666
Locals show you around for free!

9
00:00:30,690 --> 00:00:33,779
They guide us for free?

10
00:00:33,802 --> 00:00:36,369
That’s amazing!

11
00:00:36,392 --> 00:00:39,396
Are there English-speaking guides?

12
00:00:39,419 --> 00:00:45,077
Yes! We have guides in English and Chinese.

13
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:48,272
It’s really free? Like, zero yen?

14
00:00:48,295 --> 00:00:53,229
Yep, no fee for the guide!

15
00:00:53,252 --> 00:00:56,052
Are there any other costs?

16
00:00:56,075 --> 00:01:01,041
Just train fare and entry fees, if any.

17
00:01:01,064 --> 00:01:04,113
They’re super popular, by the way!

18
00:01:04,137 --> 00:01:06,915
Where do I book?

19
00:01:06,938 --> 00:01:10,916
At the info center or online.

20
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:13,743
Can I book for today?

21
00:01:13,766 --> 00:01:17,199
Please book before you go.

22
00:01:17,222 --> 00:01:21,189
Are there tours in Asakusa or the Imperial Palace?

23
00:01:21,212 --> 00:01:26,504
Yes! Both Asakusa and the Imperial Palace have them.

24
00:01:26,527 --> 00:01:29,727
What kind of stories will I hear?

25
00:01:29,750 --> 00:01:34,035
You’ll learn about history and architecture.

26
00:01:34,059 --> 00:01:37,192
They’ll show you great spots too!

27
00:01:37,215 --> 00:01:40,582
You can even chat with the locals!

28
00:01:40,605 --> 00:01:42,571
That’s so exciting!

29
00:01:42,594 --> 00:01:46,328
They’ll recommend delicious restaurants too!

30
00:01:46,351 --> 00:01:48,802
And you’ll learn about the culture!

31
00:01:48,825 --> 00:01:51,684
How long is one tour?

32
00:01:51,707 --> 00:01:55,841
About 1 to 2 hours.

33
00:01:55,864 --> 00:01:59,275
They’ll even take photos for you!

34
00:01:59,298 --> 00:02:01,531
That’s a perfect length!

35
00:02:01,554 --> 00:02:04,821
I’ll book for this weekend!

36
00:02:04,844 --> 00:02:08,377
Just fill in your name online.

37
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:11,697
I’d love an English-speaking guide.

38
00:02:11,721 --> 00:02:15,954
Select English in the language section.

39
00:02:15,977 --> 00:02:18,666
Will I get an email?

40
00:02:18,689 --> 00:02:22,903
Yes, you’ll get an email with the meeting spot.

41
00:02:22,927 --> 00:02:25,894
I’ll check the email and head there!

42
00:02:25,917 --> 00:02:28,974
Thanks for sharing the news!

43
00:02:28,997 --> 00:02:31,770
Hope you have a great time!

44
00:02:31,794 --> 00:02:40,803
You can download today’s video script from the description and top comment. Don’t forget to leave a comment before downloading!

45
00:02:40,803 --> 00:02:42,303
Scene 2: Booking a Free English Guide – Step-by-Step

46
00:02:42,303 --> 00:02:44,073
Excuse me.

47
00:02:44,096 --> 00:02:48,916
I’d like to book a free English-guided tour.

48
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:50,606
Welcome!

49
00:02:50,629 --> 00:02:53,034
This is the guide reception.

50
00:02:53,058 --> 00:02:56,748
Do you have a tour tomorrow morning?

51
00:02:56,771 --> 00:02:58,238
Yes.

52
00:02:58,261 --> 00:03:02,140
We have a tour tomorrow at 10 AM.

53
00:03:02,163 --> 00:03:05,196
Where will we be guided?

54
00:03:05,219 --> 00:03:08,886
We'll explore Asakusa and visit Senso-ji Temple.

55
00:03:08,909 --> 00:03:11,709
How long is the tour?

56
00:03:11,732 --> 00:03:14,265
About two hours.

57
00:03:14,288 --> 00:03:16,925
Is the guide English-speaking?

58
00:03:16,949 --> 00:03:18,482
Yes.

59
00:03:18,505 --> 00:03:20,972
Yes, the guide speaks English.

60
00:03:20,995 --> 00:03:24,533
Is the guide service free?

61
00:03:24,556 --> 00:03:25,889
Yes.

62
00:03:25,912 --> 00:03:28,048
Yes, it's free.

63
00:03:28,072 --> 00:03:30,115
That’s so exciting!

64
00:03:30,138 --> 00:03:34,230
You just need to cover train fares and entrance fees.

65
00:03:34,254 --> 00:03:36,287
Got it.

66
00:03:36,310 --> 00:03:38,512
Two of us will be going.

67
00:03:38,536 --> 00:03:41,411
Please write your names on this paper.

68
00:03:41,435 --> 00:03:45,568
I'll write my name and my friend's name.

69
00:03:45,591 --> 00:03:48,424
Please include your hotel name as well.

70
00:03:48,447 --> 00:03:51,332
I've written the hotel name.

71
00:03:51,355 --> 00:03:53,235
Confirmed.

72
00:03:53,258 --> 00:03:55,125
Thank you.

73
00:03:55,148 --> 00:03:58,916
Where should we meet tomorrow?

74
00:03:58,939 --> 00:04:03,873
Please come to the front of the red flag by 9:50 AM.

75
00:04:03,896 --> 00:04:06,062
The red flag, right?

76
00:04:06,085 --> 00:04:07,862
Got it.

77
00:04:07,886 --> 00:04:11,302
The guide will be holding a sign.

78
00:04:11,326 --> 00:04:13,693
Should we wear sneakers?

79
00:04:13,716 --> 00:04:15,082
Yes.

80
00:04:15,105 --> 00:04:17,872
Please wear comfortable walking shoes.

81
00:04:17,895 --> 00:04:20,895
I'll bring water and a hat.

82
00:04:20,918 --> 00:04:24,566
It'll be hot, so make sure to stay hydrated.

83
00:04:24,589 --> 00:04:28,163
Can we have photos taken for us?

84
00:04:28,187 --> 00:04:29,557
Yes.

85
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:32,747
The guide will take plenty of photos.

86
00:04:32,770 --> 00:04:35,807
I'm excited to learn about the history.

87
00:04:35,830 --> 00:04:39,066
You'll discover some fascinating history.

88
00:04:39,089 --> 00:04:41,823
I'd also like to know about good places to eat.

89
00:04:41,846 --> 00:04:45,279
The guide will recommend places like ramen shops.

90
00:04:45,302 --> 00:04:48,035
Can I get a handout?

91
00:04:48,058 --> 00:04:49,492
Yes.

92
00:04:49,516 --> 00:04:51,994
I'll give you a guide sheet.

93
00:04:52,018 --> 00:04:54,664
I'll take good care of it.

94
00:04:54,688 --> 00:04:57,984
We'll be waiting for you at 9:50 AM tomorrow.

95
00:04:58,007 --> 00:04:59,774
Thank you very much.

96
00:04:59,797 --> 00:05:01,763
Looking forward to it.

97
00:05:01,786 --> 00:05:08,891
You can review today's video with the link in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without prior notice.

98
00:05:08,891 --> 00:05:10,391
Scene 3: How to Register Your Move

99
00:05:10,391 --> 00:05:12,325
Excuse me.

100
00:05:12,348 --> 00:05:15,840
I'd like to register my move.

101
00:05:15,864 --> 00:05:17,000
Yes.

102
00:05:17,023 --> 00:05:19,714
Please proceed to this counter.

103
00:05:19,738 --> 00:05:23,105
I've just moved to this new city.

104
00:05:23,128 --> 00:05:27,867
Please write your new address on this form.

105
00:05:27,891 --> 00:05:30,373
Should I write it in kanji?

106
00:05:30,397 --> 00:05:33,930
Please write it in both kanji and katakana.

107
00:05:33,953 --> 00:05:36,720
Should I include the room number?

108
00:05:36,743 --> 00:05:38,310
Yes.

109
00:05:38,333 --> 00:05:41,145
Please include the room number as well.

110
00:05:41,168 --> 00:05:44,137
Should I write the date I moved?

111
00:05:44,161 --> 00:05:45,656
Yes.

112
00:05:45,679 --> 00:05:50,287
Write about the day you moved into your new home.

113
00:05:50,311 --> 00:05:53,362
I wrote July 20th.

114
00:05:53,386 --> 00:05:56,453
Do you have the paperwork from your previous town?

115
00:05:56,476 --> 00:05:57,769
Yes.

116
00:05:57,793 --> 00:06:01,861
I have the paperwork from my previous town and my residence card.

117
00:06:01,885 --> 00:06:04,724
I’ll take the documents and the card.

118
00:06:04,747 --> 00:06:09,347
Should I write my new address on the back of the residence card?

119
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:10,838
Yes.

120
00:06:10,862 --> 00:06:14,228
You can write your new address here.

121
00:06:14,251 --> 00:06:18,785
Do I also need to update the address on my My Number Card?

122
00:06:18,807 --> 00:06:20,249
Yes.

123
00:06:20,273 --> 00:06:22,207
We’ll update it together.

124
00:06:22,230 --> 00:06:24,630
Please hand over your card.

125
00:06:24,653 --> 00:06:27,086
Do I need to enter the password?

126
00:06:27,109 --> 00:06:30,842
Please enter your 4-digit password.

127
00:06:30,865 --> 00:06:33,232
I’ve entered the password.

128
00:06:33,255 --> 00:06:36,455
Your card has been updated!

129
00:06:36,478 --> 00:06:39,811
May I get a copy of my address certificate?

130
00:06:39,834 --> 00:06:41,401
Yes.

131
00:06:41,425 --> 00:06:43,898
I’ll print out your address certificate.

132
00:06:43,921 --> 00:06:46,288
How much is one copy?

133
00:06:46,311 --> 00:06:49,121
It’s 300 yen per copy.

134
00:06:49,144 --> 00:06:51,077
I’ll take two, please.

135
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:53,903
That’ll be 600 yen for two copies.

136
00:06:53,927 --> 00:06:56,802
Here’s 600 yen in cash.

137
00:06:56,826 --> 00:06:59,764
Here are your two copies.

138
00:06:59,787 --> 00:07:01,320
Thank you.

139
00:07:01,343 --> 00:07:04,177
I’ll also give you the garbage collection guide.

140
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:07,298
Could I get an English version of the guide?

141
00:07:07,321 --> 00:07:08,755
Yes.

142
00:07:08,778 --> 00:07:11,111
Here’s the English version for you.

143
00:07:11,134 --> 00:07:13,414
Check the collection days before taking out the trash.

144
00:07:13,437 --> 00:07:16,171
Please make sure to check the days.

145
00:07:16,194 --> 00:07:18,827
Thank you so much for your help!

146
00:07:18,850 --> 00:07:22,326
Enjoy your new life!

147
00:07:22,349 --> 00:07:23,849
Scene 4: My Number Card Pickup Procedure

148
00:07:23,849 --> 00:07:26,016
Excuse me.

149
00:07:26,039 --> 00:07:29,442
I’d like to pick up my My Number Card.

150
00:07:29,465 --> 00:07:32,032
Please proceed to the card counter.

151
00:07:32,055 --> 00:07:34,730
I received a pink postcard.

152
00:07:34,753 --> 00:07:36,820
I’ll take the postcard.

153
00:07:36,843 --> 00:07:39,488
Do you have your residence card?

154
00:07:39,511 --> 00:07:42,678
I have my residence card and passport.

155
00:07:42,701 --> 00:07:44,308
I’ve reviewed them.

156
00:07:44,331 --> 00:07:45,944
Everything looks good.

157
00:07:45,967 --> 00:07:49,167
I’ve written my name on the back of the postcard.

158
00:07:49,190 --> 00:07:50,969
Thank you.

159
00:07:50,993 --> 00:07:53,726
Do I need to set a password?

160
00:07:53,749 --> 00:07:54,818
Yes.

161
00:07:54,842 --> 00:07:57,242
Please set your password.

162
00:07:57,265 --> 00:08:00,065
How many passwords do I need?

163
00:08:00,088 --> 00:08:05,254
You’ll need a 4-digit PIN and an alphanumeric password.

164
00:08:05,277 --> 00:08:09,089
Is the 4-digit PIN used at convenience stores?

165
00:08:09,113 --> 00:08:10,086
Yes.

166
00:08:10,109 --> 00:08:14,243
Yes, for example, when printing address certificates at a convenience store.

167
00:08:14,266 --> 00:08:17,068
I’ll enter the 4-digit PIN now.

168
00:08:17,091 --> 00:08:19,110
Please enter it on the screen.

169
00:08:19,133 --> 00:08:20,700
I’ve entered it.

170
00:08:20,723 --> 00:08:23,798
Next is the longer password.

171
00:08:23,821 --> 00:08:25,056
Yes.

172
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:27,715
Please enter a combination of letters and numbers.

173
00:08:27,739 --> 00:08:29,911
I’ve entered the password.

174
00:08:29,934 --> 00:08:31,934
It's all done.

175
00:08:31,957 --> 00:08:33,690
I'll write it down in the memo.

176
00:08:33,713 --> 00:08:36,480
Please keep it safe.

177
00:08:36,503 --> 00:08:38,750
How long is this card valid?

178
00:08:38,773 --> 00:08:44,251
It's valid until the same day as your residence card.

179
00:08:44,275 --> 00:08:46,242
What should I do when my residence card is renewed?

180
00:08:46,265 --> 00:08:48,832
You'll need to renew this card as well.

181
00:08:48,855 --> 00:08:52,988
Do I have to come to the ward office then?

182
00:08:53,011 --> 00:08:54,186
Yes.

183
00:08:54,209 --> 00:08:56,083
Please do come in.

184
00:08:56,107 --> 00:08:57,574
Got it.

185
00:08:57,597 --> 00:09:00,637
Now, let's verify your face.

186
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:03,060
Should I take off my mask?

187
00:09:03,083 --> 00:09:04,250
Yes.

188
00:09:04,273 --> 00:09:08,106
Please look at the camera and remove your mask.

189
00:09:08,129 --> 00:09:09,701
I've taken it off.

190
00:09:09,724 --> 00:09:11,024
Yes.

191
00:09:11,047 --> 00:09:12,714
Verification complete.

192
00:09:12,737 --> 00:09:14,782
I'll hand you the card now.

193
00:09:14,805 --> 00:09:16,810
I've received the card.

194
00:09:16,834 --> 00:09:19,967
This also works as a hospital card, you know.

195
00:09:19,991 --> 00:09:22,563
You can use it at hospitals.

196
00:09:22,587 --> 00:09:24,191
That's convenient!

197
00:09:24,214 --> 00:09:26,427
Please use the app as well.

198
00:09:26,450 --> 00:09:28,817
I'll install the app.

199
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:31,718
If you lose it, please give us a call.

200
00:09:31,742 --> 00:09:33,624
I'll keep it in my wallet.

201
00:09:33,648 --> 00:09:35,983
Thank you very much.

202
00:09:36,006 --> 00:09:37,506
Scene 5: Introduction to the Japanese Language Class

203
00:09:37,506 --> 00:09:39,483
Excuse me.

204
00:09:39,506 --> 00:09:43,673
Could you tell me about the Japanese language class?

205
00:09:43,696 --> 00:09:44,786
Sure!

206
00:09:44,810 --> 00:09:48,223
Here's the information about our Japanese class.

207
00:09:48,246 --> 00:09:53,057
Can I study Japanese here?

208
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:54,366
Sure!

209
00:09:54,389 --> 00:09:58,127
We hold classes every Saturday.

210
00:09:58,151 --> 00:10:00,888
What time do they start?

211
00:10:00,911 --> 00:10:05,550
From 10:00 AM to 11:30 AM.

212
00:10:05,574 --> 00:10:08,040
How much does it cost?

213
00:10:08,063 --> 00:10:10,997
It's free of charge.

214
00:10:11,020 --> 00:10:12,864
Free?

215
00:10:12,887 --> 00:10:14,978
That’s so exciting!

216
00:10:15,001 --> 00:10:19,614
You only need to pay 500 yen for the textbook.

217
00:10:19,637 --> 00:10:21,448
500 yen, got it.

218
00:10:21,471 --> 00:10:24,205
What kind of textbook is it?

219
00:10:24,228 --> 00:10:29,233
It's an N5-level textbook for beginners.

220
00:10:29,256 --> 00:10:33,056
Can I start learning hiragana from scratch?

221
00:10:33,079 --> 00:10:34,957
Sure!

222
00:10:34,981 --> 00:10:37,648
We teach hiragana from the very beginning.

223
00:10:37,671 --> 00:10:40,568
Are the teachers volunteers?

224
00:10:40,591 --> 00:10:42,524
Sure!

225
00:10:42,547 --> 00:10:45,914
Yes, they're kind volunteer teachers.

226
00:10:45,937 --> 00:10:48,504
Is there just one teacher?

227
00:10:48,527 --> 00:10:53,368
There's one teacher for every two students.

228
00:10:53,391 --> 00:10:56,027
That's great for asking questions!

229
00:10:56,050 --> 00:10:59,858
You'll get plenty of speaking practice.

230
00:10:59,882 --> 00:11:02,759
Can I bring my child along?

231
00:11:02,782 --> 00:11:04,516
Sure!

232
00:11:04,539 --> 00:11:07,432
There's a play area for children.

233
00:11:07,455 --> 00:11:10,501
You can come with peace of mind.

234
00:11:10,525 --> 00:11:14,006
You can even observe a class first!

235
00:11:14,029 --> 00:11:16,432
I want to watch it this Saturday.

236
00:11:16,456 --> 00:11:19,462
You can watch it anytime.

237
00:11:19,486 --> 00:11:23,381
I’ll come this Saturday at 10 AM.

238
00:11:23,404 --> 00:11:28,138
Please come to the counter at 9:45.

239
00:11:28,161 --> 00:11:30,235
Should I write my name?

240
00:11:30,258 --> 00:11:31,825
Sure!

241
00:11:31,848 --> 00:11:36,621
Please write your name and phone number on this paper.

242
00:11:36,645 --> 00:11:39,616
Name and phone number, right?

243
00:11:39,639 --> 00:11:41,806
I’ve written it down.

244
00:11:41,829 --> 00:11:43,429
Thank you very much.

245
00:11:43,452 --> 00:11:46,629
I’m excited to go to the classroom!

246
00:11:46,652 --> 00:11:50,019
Let’s have fun studying Japanese!

247
00:11:50,042 --> 00:11:53,209
Can I go with my friend?

248
00:11:53,233 --> 00:11:54,866
Sure!

249
00:11:54,889 --> 00:11:57,184
Please come with your friend.

250
00:11:57,208 --> 00:11:58,902
Thank you very much.

251
00:11:58,925 --> 00:12:02,658
I’ll be waiting for you this Saturday!

252
00:12:02,681 --> 00:12:03,681
Sure!

253
00:12:03,704 --> 00:12:05,985
I’ll go this Saturday.

254
00:12:06,009 --> 00:12:07,862
Goodbye.

255
00:12:07,885 --> 00:12:09,385
Scene 6: Shinkansen Luggage Reservation Rules

256
00:12:09,385 --> 00:12:12,919
Did you catch the morning news?

257
00:12:12,942 --> 00:12:16,075
No, I didn’t.

258
00:12:16,098 --> 00:12:20,331
News about large luggage on the Shinkansen.

259
00:12:20,354 --> 00:12:22,888
What’s the news?

260
00:12:22,911 --> 00:12:27,890
You need to reserve space for large suitcases.

261
00:12:27,913 --> 00:12:31,331
Do I make the reservation before boarding?

262
00:12:31,355 --> 00:12:34,767
Yes, a reservation is required.

263
00:12:34,790 --> 00:12:39,023
What happens if I forget to reserve?

264
00:12:39,046 --> 00:12:41,980
You’ll have to pay 1,000 yen.

265
00:12:42,003 --> 00:12:45,010
1,000 yen? That’s expensive!

266
00:12:45,033 --> 00:12:48,600
Yes, so please be careful.

267
00:12:48,624 --> 00:12:51,500
Where can I make a reservation?

268
00:12:51,524 --> 00:12:54,800
You can reserve at the counter.

269
00:12:54,823 --> 00:12:59,057
Can I reserve at the ticket machine too?

270
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:03,564
Yes, you can reserve at the ticket machine as well.

271
00:13:03,587 --> 00:13:06,220
Can I do it online too?

272
00:13:06,243 --> 00:13:10,510
Yes, you can even reserve with your smartphone.

273
00:13:10,533 --> 00:13:13,699
Where do I put my luggage?

274
00:13:13,722 --> 00:13:17,335
Behind the last row of seats.

275
00:13:17,359 --> 00:13:21,126
The seats for large luggage, right?

276
00:13:21,149 --> 00:13:24,715
Yes, those seats.

277
00:13:24,738 --> 00:13:28,472
Do those seats cost extra?

278
00:13:28,495 --> 00:13:31,380
No, they’re free.

279
00:13:31,403 --> 00:13:35,136
Free? That’s a relief!

280
00:13:35,159 --> 00:13:38,036
What about non-reserved seats?

281
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:40,894
Non-reserved seats aren’t allowed.

282
00:13:40,917 --> 00:13:44,574
Then I’ll buy a reserved seat.

283
00:13:44,597 --> 00:13:47,997
Yes, please buy a reserved seat.

284
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:52,687
I’ll measure my luggage at home.

285
00:13:52,710 --> 00:13:56,889
You don’t need a reservation if it’s under 160 cm.

286
00:13:56,913 --> 00:14:01,480
In that case, I’ll put it on the overhead rack.

287
00:14:01,503 --> 00:14:04,240
Yes, put it up there.

288
00:14:04,263 --> 00:14:05,946
Got it.

289
00:14:05,969 --> 00:14:07,836
That’s great.

290
00:14:07,859 --> 00:14:09,592
I’ll be careful.

291
00:14:09,615 --> 00:14:12,817
Enjoy your trip!

292
00:14:12,841 --> 00:14:14,848
Thank you.

293
00:14:14,872 --> 00:14:16,605
I'm off.

294
00:14:16,628 --> 00:14:18,862
Take care. See you later.

295
00:14:18,885 --> 00:14:20,385
Scene 7: How to Buy a Train Ticket

296
00:14:20,385 --> 00:14:22,060
Excuse me.

297
00:14:22,083 --> 00:14:24,725
I'd like to buy a ticket.

298
00:14:24,748 --> 00:14:26,382
Welcome!

299
00:14:26,405 --> 00:14:28,771
Where are you headed?

300
00:14:28,794 --> 00:14:32,165
From Tokyo to Kyoto.

301
00:14:32,189 --> 00:14:34,756
What time would you like to take today?

302
00:14:34,779 --> 00:14:38,312
The 10 AM train, please.

303
00:14:38,335 --> 00:14:39,902
Yes.

304
00:14:39,925 --> 00:14:43,613
There's a Nozomi train at 10:07 AM.

305
00:14:43,636 --> 00:14:45,836
Two adults, please.

306
00:14:45,859 --> 00:14:47,293
Yes.

307
00:14:47,316 --> 00:14:48,920
Reserved seats, correct?

308
00:14:48,943 --> 00:14:52,677
We have two large suitcases.

309
00:14:52,700 --> 00:14:56,833
Are your bags larger than 160 centimeters?

310
00:14:56,856 --> 00:14:58,223
Yes.

311
00:14:58,246 --> 00:15:01,012
They're 180 centimeters.

312
00:15:01,035 --> 00:15:04,878
Then I'll assign you seats for large luggage.

313
00:15:04,902 --> 00:15:07,573
What kind of seats are those?

314
00:15:07,597 --> 00:15:10,453
They're at the very back.

315
00:15:10,476 --> 00:15:14,076
You can place your luggage behind the seats.

316
00:15:14,099 --> 00:15:16,739
Will it cost extra?

317
00:15:16,762 --> 00:15:19,647
No, it's the same price.

318
00:15:19,671 --> 00:15:21,748
Same price?

319
00:15:21,772 --> 00:15:23,779
That’s so exciting!

320
00:15:23,802 --> 00:15:26,936
I'll assign you seats D and E.

321
00:15:26,959 --> 00:15:29,374
They're next to each other.

322
00:15:29,397 --> 00:15:32,335
We'd prefer seats near the window.

323
00:15:32,358 --> 00:15:35,170
Seat E is closer to the window.

324
00:15:35,193 --> 00:15:38,281
We'll take those seats, please.

325
00:15:38,305 --> 00:15:41,472
That'll be 14,000 yen per person.

326
00:15:41,495 --> 00:15:44,392
So, 28,000 yen for two, right?

327
00:15:44,416 --> 00:15:45,709
Yes.

328
00:15:45,732 --> 00:15:48,299
That's correct, 28,000 yen.

329
00:15:48,322 --> 00:15:50,289
I'll pay by card.

330
00:15:50,312 --> 00:15:53,602
Please tap your card here.

331
00:15:53,625 --> 00:15:54,825
Yes.

332
00:15:54,848 --> 00:15:57,421
Four tickets will be issued.

333
00:15:57,445 --> 00:15:59,582
Two tickets per person, correct?

334
00:15:59,605 --> 00:16:00,901
Yes.

335
00:16:00,924 --> 00:16:04,339
Insert both tickets together at the ticket gate.

336
00:16:04,363 --> 00:16:05,999
Got it.

337
00:16:06,022 --> 00:16:07,869
I'll insert both.

338
00:16:07,893 --> 00:16:11,362
The train departs from Platform 16.

339
00:16:11,386 --> 00:16:14,031
Where do I put my luggage?

340
00:16:14,054 --> 00:16:17,288
Please place your luggage behind your seat.

341
00:16:17,311 --> 00:16:18,444
Yes.

342
00:16:18,467 --> 00:16:20,555
I'll put it behind.

343
00:16:20,579 --> 00:16:24,184
Make sure to write your name on your luggage.

344
00:16:24,207 --> 00:16:25,374
Yes.

345
00:16:25,397 --> 00:16:27,771
I'll attach a name tag.

346
00:16:27,794 --> 00:16:29,761
That's all for now.

347
00:16:29,784 --> 00:16:31,451
Thank you very much.

348
00:16:31,474 --> 00:16:34,147
Have a great trip!

349
00:16:34,171 --> 00:16:35,671
Scene 8: How to Change Your Train Ticket Time

350
00:16:35,671 --> 00:16:41,004
Excuse me, I'd like to change the time on my ticket.

351
00:16:41,027 --> 00:16:45,106
Sure, you can do that at the machine over there.

352
00:16:45,130 --> 00:16:50,263
I'll press 'English' on the screen.

353
00:16:50,286 --> 00:16:53,890
Great, now it's in English.

354
00:16:53,914 --> 00:16:57,767
I'll select 'Change Time'.

355
00:16:57,791 --> 00:17:03,087
Okay, next please insert the ticket you have.

356
00:17:03,110 --> 00:17:05,977
I'll insert it here.

357
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,538
Yes, your ticket has been issued.

358
00:17:09,561 --> 00:17:14,596
I’ll change your train from 11:00 to 12:00.

359
00:17:14,619 --> 00:17:17,597
The first change is free of charge.

360
00:17:17,621 --> 00:17:19,387
Free?

361
00:17:19,410 --> 00:17:21,777
That’s so exciting!

362
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:25,210
Please select the 12:00 train.

363
00:17:25,233 --> 00:17:29,636
I’ll go with the 12:05 Nozomi train.

364
00:17:29,659 --> 00:17:32,798
Do you have any large luggage?

365
00:17:32,822 --> 00:17:37,316
Yes, I have a very large piece of luggage.

366
00:17:37,339 --> 00:17:42,106
Please press the button for seats with large luggage space.

367
00:17:42,129 --> 00:17:44,781
Yes, I pressed it.

368
00:17:44,804 --> 00:17:50,804
Seats 15D and 15E at the very back are available.

369
00:17:50,827 --> 00:17:54,760
I’ll take 15D and 15E.

370
00:17:54,783 --> 00:17:58,021
Those are seats where you can place your luggage behind you, right?

371
00:17:58,045 --> 00:18:01,479
Please press the confirm button.

372
00:18:01,501 --> 00:18:03,068
I pressed it.

373
00:18:03,091 --> 00:18:05,986
Will this cost extra?

374
00:18:06,010 --> 00:18:09,029
No, it won’t.

375
00:18:09,052 --> 00:18:11,185
That’s great.

376
00:18:11,208 --> 00:18:14,475
Your new ticket will come out now.

377
00:18:14,498 --> 00:18:16,665
Here’s your ticket.

378
00:18:16,688 --> 00:18:20,654
Your old ticket will be taken by the machine.

379
00:18:20,677 --> 00:18:26,811
Your new ticket says 'Large Luggage' on it.

380
00:18:26,834 --> 00:18:29,567
You did it correctly!

381
00:18:29,590 --> 00:18:33,323
You have an hour until your train departs.

382
00:18:33,346 --> 00:18:36,039
Why not relax at the café?

383
00:18:36,062 --> 00:18:38,940
I’ll grab some tea and wait.

384
00:18:38,964 --> 00:18:42,968
Your train will depart from Platform 16.

385
00:18:42,992 --> 00:18:46,562
Got it, I’ll head to Platform 16.

386
00:18:46,586 --> 00:18:50,828
Please insert your new ticket at the ticket gate.

387
00:18:50,851 --> 00:18:52,823
Got it.

388
00:18:52,847 --> 00:18:58,013
Place your luggage behind seat 15.

389
00:18:58,036 --> 00:19:00,674
I’ll remember that.

390
00:19:00,697 --> 00:19:03,180
Have a safe trip!

391
00:19:03,204 --> 00:19:04,704
Scene 9: How to Store Luggage at Your Seat

392
00:19:04,704 --> 00:19:06,538
Excuse me.

393
00:19:06,562 --> 00:19:10,928
Where should I put my large luggage?

394
00:19:10,951 --> 00:19:13,801
What’s your seat number?

395
00:19:13,825 --> 00:19:18,625
Seats 15D and 15E.

396
00:19:18,648 --> 00:19:21,685
Behind seat 15.

397
00:19:21,708 --> 00:19:24,515
Behind the seat, right?

398
00:19:24,539 --> 00:19:25,872
Sure!

399
00:19:25,895 --> 00:19:29,179
Please place your suitcase there.

400
00:19:29,203 --> 00:19:32,272
Can I place two suitcases there?

401
00:19:32,295 --> 00:19:33,582
Sure!

402
00:19:33,605 --> 00:19:36,438
Yes, you can place two.

403
00:19:36,461 --> 00:19:38,530
Will they fall over?

404
00:19:38,554 --> 00:19:41,032
Please lock the wheels.

405
00:19:41,055 --> 00:19:42,702
I locked them.

406
00:19:42,726 --> 00:19:45,560
Now you can relax!

407
00:19:45,583 --> 00:19:48,755
Should I lock my luggage?

408
00:19:48,778 --> 00:19:52,218
Since I’m worried, please lock it.

409
00:19:52,242 --> 00:19:53,575
Sure!

410
00:19:53,598 --> 00:19:55,798
I’ll lock it.

411
00:19:55,821 --> 00:19:59,754
After placing your luggage, please take your seat.

412
00:19:59,777 --> 00:20:03,111
I’ll sit in seat 15D.

413
00:20:03,134 --> 00:20:05,667
Please relax and enjoy your ride.

414
00:20:05,690 --> 00:20:09,490
Is there Wi-Fi on the train?

415
00:20:09,513 --> 00:20:10,880
Sure!

416
00:20:10,903 --> 00:20:13,269
Free Wi-Fi available.

417
00:20:13,292 --> 00:20:16,059
Let me connect my phone.

418
00:20:16,082 --> 00:20:19,649
Please press the 'Yes' button on the screen.

419
00:20:19,671 --> 00:20:22,647
You're now connected to the internet.

420
00:20:22,670 --> 00:20:26,165
There are also power outlets under your seat.

421
00:20:26,188 --> 00:20:28,155
I'll charge my phone.

422
00:20:28,178 --> 00:20:29,611
Sure!

423
00:20:29,634 --> 00:20:32,034
You can charge your phone here.

424
00:20:32,057 --> 00:20:35,257
Will the person selling bento boxes come by?

425
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:38,882
The vendor only comes to the Green Car.

426
00:20:38,906 --> 00:20:43,439
Can I buy a bento box at this seat?

427
00:20:43,462 --> 00:20:46,829
You can order using your smartphone.

428
00:20:46,852 --> 00:20:50,885
I'll use the QR code at the seat.

429
00:20:50,908 --> 00:20:51,908
Sure!

430
00:20:51,931 --> 00:20:55,498
You can also buy ice cream and coffee.

431
00:20:55,521 --> 00:20:58,454
I'll get some ice cream.

432
00:20:58,477 --> 00:21:01,611
It's the famous Shinkansen ice cream—so good!

433
00:21:01,634 --> 00:21:03,671
I can't wait!

434
00:21:03,694 --> 00:21:07,111
We still have two hours until Kyoto.

435
00:21:07,135 --> 00:21:09,501
This train is so quiet.

436
00:21:09,524 --> 00:21:12,658
Let me know if you need anything.

437
00:21:12,681 --> 00:21:14,361
Thank you very much.

438
00:21:14,384 --> 00:21:17,078
Have a great trip!

439
00:21:17,102 --> 00:21:18,602
Scene 10: Reserving and Fees for Oversized Luggage

440
00:21:18,602 --> 00:21:23,735
Excuse me, I don’t know where to put my suitcase.

441
00:21:23,758 --> 00:21:26,292
May I see your ticket, please?

442
00:21:26,315 --> 00:21:30,281
Car 8, Seat 10A.

443
00:21:30,304 --> 00:21:33,104
That’s a large piece of luggage.

444
00:21:33,127 --> 00:21:36,460
Yes, it’s 180 centimeters.

445
00:21:36,483 --> 00:21:41,735
Luggage over 160 centimeters is considered oversized.

446
00:21:41,759 --> 00:21:45,765
Did I need to reserve a spot for it before boarding?

447
00:21:45,788 --> 00:21:49,365
Yes, a reservation is required.

448
00:21:49,388 --> 00:21:52,221
I forgot to make a reservation.

449
00:21:52,244 --> 00:21:56,702
There’s a fee if you don’t have a reservation.

450
00:21:56,726 --> 00:21:58,660
How much is it?

451
00:21:58,683 --> 00:22:01,097
It’s 1,000 yen.

452
00:22:01,121 --> 00:22:03,454
Will you pay in cash?

453
00:22:03,477 --> 00:22:07,013
Yes, I’ll pay in cash.

454
00:22:07,037 --> 00:22:09,437
That’ll be 1,000 yen, please.

455
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:11,526
Here’s your receipt.

456
00:22:11,549 --> 00:22:14,216
Got the receipt.

457
00:22:14,239 --> 00:22:17,520
Where do I put my luggage?

458
00:22:17,544 --> 00:22:23,121
Please place it behind Seat 15 at the very back.

459
00:22:23,145 --> 00:22:26,804
Behind Seat 15, right?

460
00:22:26,827 --> 00:22:30,795
Just put it in any available space.

461
00:22:30,819 --> 00:22:33,552
I’ve placed my luggage.

462
00:22:33,575 --> 00:22:35,950
Please lock the wheels.

463
00:22:35,973 --> 00:22:37,977
I locked them.

464
00:22:38,001 --> 00:22:42,481
Next time, please make a reservation before boarding.

465
00:22:42,505 --> 00:22:45,238
Is the reservation free?

466
00:22:45,261 --> 00:22:48,340
Yes, it’s free.

467
00:22:48,364 --> 00:22:51,536
Can I reserve online?

468
00:22:51,559 --> 00:22:55,802
You can reserve via the website or app.

469
00:22:55,825 --> 00:22:58,911
I’ll make sure to reserve next time.

470
00:22:58,935 --> 00:23:05,945
Luggage over 250 centimeters cannot be brought on board.

471
00:23:05,968 --> 00:23:11,535
My luggage is 180 centimeters, so it’s okay, right?

472
00:23:11,559 --> 00:23:14,613
Yes, that’s fine.

473
00:23:14,637 --> 00:23:17,323
I’ll head back to my seat.

474
00:23:17,346 --> 00:23:21,785
Please return to seat 10A in Car No. 8.

475
00:23:21,809 --> 00:23:25,542
I'll use the Wi-Fi on the train.

476
00:23:25,565 --> 00:23:28,931
Press 'Yes' to connect.

477
00:23:28,954 --> 00:23:30,621
Thank you.

478
00:23:30,645 --> 00:23:32,978
Please relax and enjoy your ride.

479
00:23:33,001 --> 00:23:36,207
Yes, thank you.

480
00:23:36,230 --> 00:23:39,230
Excuse me.

481
00:23:39,253 --> 00:23:40,753
Scene 11: What Is a Cooling Shelter?

482
00:23:40,753 --> 00:23:44,153
Did you catch the morning news?

483
00:23:44,176 --> 00:23:47,576
No, I didn’t.

484
00:23:47,599 --> 00:23:50,811
News about cooling shelters.

485
00:23:50,834 --> 00:23:54,471
What is a cooling shelter?

486
00:23:54,494 --> 00:23:59,828
It's a cool place where you can rest for free.

487
00:23:59,852 --> 00:24:03,052
A free cool place to rest?

488
00:24:03,074 --> 00:24:04,885
That sounds great!

489
00:24:04,909 --> 00:24:07,243
Where can I find them?

490
00:24:07,266 --> 00:24:10,555
They're in libraries and department stores.

491
00:24:10,578 --> 00:24:13,858
Can anyone enter freely?

492
00:24:13,881 --> 00:24:17,653
Yes, anyone can go in.

493
00:24:17,676 --> 00:24:20,843
What kind of sign do they have?

494
00:24:20,867 --> 00:24:23,515
There’s a blue sticker.

495
00:24:23,539 --> 00:24:26,574
I’ll look for the sticker.

496
00:24:26,597 --> 00:24:30,731
It’s very hot outside, so please be careful.

497
00:24:30,754 --> 00:24:33,887
Now even hot days are manageable!

498
00:24:33,910 --> 00:24:36,443
Do they have water?

499
00:24:36,466 --> 00:24:39,799
Yes, they have cold water.

500
00:24:39,822 --> 00:24:43,056
Can I sit on a chair too?

501
00:24:43,079 --> 00:24:46,699
Yes, you can rest in a chair.

502
00:24:46,723 --> 00:24:49,809
Hot days are no longer a worry!

503
00:24:49,833 --> 00:24:54,288
If you're feeling unwell, go inside right away.

504
00:24:54,311 --> 00:24:58,045
Are there any in Asakusa or Ginza?

505
00:24:58,068 --> 00:25:01,468
Yes, there are plenty!

506
00:25:01,491 --> 00:25:04,458
Can I borrow a sun umbrella?

507
00:25:04,481 --> 00:25:09,014
You can borrow one for free at the information desk.

508
00:25:09,037 --> 00:25:12,004
Sun umbrellas are so cooling!

509
00:25:12,027 --> 00:25:14,994
Don’t forget to wear a hat too.

510
00:25:15,017 --> 00:25:17,711
I’ll have some salt candy too.

511
00:25:17,735 --> 00:25:19,975
You’re well-prepared!

512
00:25:19,998 --> 00:25:23,269
Can I find the locations online?

513
00:25:23,293 --> 00:25:27,893
Yes, you can check the city’s website for a map.

514
00:25:27,916 --> 00:25:31,482
I’ll check the map before my walk.

515
00:25:31,505 --> 00:25:34,564
I’ll tell my friends too.

516
00:25:34,588 --> 00:25:37,285
Knowing the locations is reassuring!

517
00:25:37,309 --> 00:25:40,709
Let’s all enjoy a cool trip together!

518
00:25:40,732 --> 00:25:44,207
Thanks for sharing the news!

519
00:25:44,230 --> 00:25:47,897
I’ll drink some water and then go for a walk.

520
00:25:47,920 --> 00:25:50,588
Take care on your walk!

521
00:25:50,611 --> 00:25:52,380
Take care. See you later.

522
00:25:52,403 --> 00:25:53,903
Scene 12: Free Sun Umbrella Rental

523
00:25:53,903 --> 00:25:59,042
Excuse me, can I borrow a sun umbrella?

524
00:25:59,066 --> 00:26:03,337
Yes, you can borrow a sun umbrella.

525
00:26:03,360 --> 00:26:05,961
How much does it cost?

526
00:26:05,985 --> 00:26:08,319
It’s free of charge.

527
00:26:08,342 --> 00:26:10,787
Yes, it's free.

528
00:26:10,810 --> 00:26:15,077
It’s so hot today, so this is great!

529
00:26:15,100 --> 00:26:19,033
Using a sun umbrella keeps you cool.

530
00:26:19,056 --> 00:26:21,704
How do I borrow one?

531
00:26:21,727 --> 00:26:25,145
Please write your names on this paper.

532
00:26:25,168 --> 00:26:28,968
Just write down your name and phone number.

533
00:26:28,991 --> 00:26:31,291
Yes, thank you.

534
00:26:31,314 --> 00:26:34,048
What colors are available?

535
00:26:34,071 --> 00:26:37,337
We have black and silver.

536
00:26:37,360 --> 00:26:40,297
I'll go with the silver parasol.

537
00:26:40,321 --> 00:26:44,138
Silver is very cooling.

538
00:26:44,162 --> 00:26:47,531
It blocks the sunlight, doesn’t it?

539
00:26:47,554 --> 00:26:51,321
Yes, you can stay cool even on hot days.

540
00:26:51,344 --> 00:26:55,077
Can I use it when it rains?

541
00:26:55,100 --> 00:26:59,568
Yes, you can use it in the rain too.

542
00:26:59,591 --> 00:27:02,643
By what time should I return it?

543
00:27:02,667 --> 00:27:07,601
Please return it by 5 PM.

544
00:27:07,624 --> 00:27:11,557
5 PM, got it.

545
00:27:11,580 --> 00:27:15,027
You can also return it in front of the station.

546
00:27:15,050 --> 00:27:17,924
Can I return it at the station?

547
00:27:17,948 --> 00:27:21,983
Yes, please return it at the station.

548
00:27:22,007 --> 00:27:25,215
That’s really convenient.

549
00:27:25,238 --> 00:27:28,287
It’ll lighten my load.

550
00:27:28,311 --> 00:27:31,844
Let me open the parasol.

551
00:27:31,867 --> 00:27:34,237
Make sure it opens properly.

552
00:27:34,260 --> 00:27:37,394
The shade feels so cool.

553
00:27:37,417 --> 00:27:41,383
Make sure to drink plenty of water too.

554
00:27:41,406 --> 00:27:45,216
Yes, I’ll be walking around Asakusa next.

555
00:27:45,240 --> 00:27:48,494
Enjoy your time in Asakusa!

556
00:27:48,517 --> 00:27:51,599
Hope you have a great trip!

557
00:27:51,623 --> 00:27:54,799
I’ll be waiting at 5 PM.

558
00:27:54,822 --> 00:27:57,756
Could I get a map of the return location?

559
00:27:57,779 --> 00:28:00,793
Here’s the map for you.

560
00:28:00,816 --> 00:28:02,449
Thank you.

561
00:28:02,472 --> 00:28:04,839
Have a nice day!

562
00:28:04,862 --> 00:28:06,362
Scene 13: Using a Cooling Shelter

563
00:28:06,362 --> 00:28:08,695
Excuse me.

564
00:28:08,718 --> 00:28:12,285
It’s so hot outside.

565
00:28:12,308 --> 00:28:15,948
Please come in and have a seat.

566
00:28:15,971 --> 00:28:19,786
Is this a cooling shelter?

567
00:28:19,809 --> 00:28:21,618
Yes.

568
00:28:21,642 --> 00:28:24,511
It’s a free place to rest.

569
00:28:24,534 --> 00:28:27,068
Please, have a seat on the sofa.

570
00:28:27,091 --> 00:28:29,361
It’s so cool in here.

571
00:28:29,385 --> 00:28:31,397
I’m glad to hear that.

572
00:28:31,420 --> 00:28:34,953
I’ll bring you some cold water.

573
00:28:34,976 --> 00:28:36,510
Here you go.

574
00:28:36,533 --> 00:28:38,533
Thank you.

575
00:28:38,556 --> 00:28:41,156
I’ll have some water.

576
00:28:41,179 --> 00:28:43,345
It’s nice and cold.

577
00:28:43,368 --> 00:28:47,255
Do you feel better now?

578
00:28:47,279 --> 00:28:49,818
Yes, I do.

579
00:28:49,841 --> 00:28:52,808
I’ll turn on the fan.

580
00:28:52,831 --> 00:28:55,564
The breeze feels great.

581
00:28:55,587 --> 00:28:58,321
Please relax and enjoy your ride.

582
00:28:58,344 --> 00:29:01,548
How long can I stay?

583
00:29:01,571 --> 00:29:04,545
You can stay as long as you like.

584
00:29:04,569 --> 00:29:07,943
I’ll rest for about an hour.

585
00:29:07,966 --> 00:29:10,899
Hope you feel refreshed!

586
00:29:10,922 --> 00:29:13,489
Is there Wi-Fi here?

587
00:29:13,512 --> 00:29:15,284
Yes.

588
00:29:15,308 --> 00:29:17,718
Free Wi-Fi available.

589
00:29:17,741 --> 00:29:21,075
I’ll check my schedule on my phone.

590
00:29:21,098 --> 00:29:24,137
There are power outlets too.

591
00:29:24,161 --> 00:29:26,740
I'll charge my phone.

592
00:29:26,763 --> 00:29:29,497
We also have a thermometer.

593
00:29:29,520 --> 00:29:32,409
May I take your temperature?

594
00:29:32,432 --> 00:29:34,232
Yes.

595
00:29:34,256 --> 00:29:36,791
Please take your temperature.

596
00:29:36,815 --> 00:29:39,690
It's 36.5 degrees.

597
00:29:39,713 --> 00:29:41,713
You're all good.

598
00:29:41,736 --> 00:29:43,936
I’m glad to hear that.

599
00:29:43,959 --> 00:29:45,726
That's a relief.

600
00:29:45,749 --> 00:29:48,994
I'm heading outside soon.

601
00:29:49,018 --> 00:29:53,851
Please wear a hat when you go outside.

602
00:29:53,874 --> 00:29:56,541
I'll have some salt candy.

603
00:29:56,564 --> 00:29:58,497
Perfect!

604
00:29:58,520 --> 00:30:02,208
I’m glad to hear that.

605
00:30:02,232 --> 00:30:03,799
Thank you.

606
00:30:03,821 --> 00:30:08,688
There are plenty of places to rest in the city.

607
00:30:08,711 --> 00:30:11,564
Could I get a map?

608
00:30:11,587 --> 00:30:13,220
Yes.

609
00:30:13,243 --> 00:30:15,895
Here's the map for you.

610
00:30:15,919 --> 00:30:17,495
Thank you.

611
00:30:17,519 --> 00:30:19,692
Have a nice day!

612
00:30:19,716 --> 00:30:21,216
Scene 14: How to Use a Water Refill Station

613
00:30:21,216 --> 00:30:23,382
Excuse me.

614
00:30:23,405 --> 00:30:27,444
Can I fill my bottle with water here?

615
00:30:27,468 --> 00:30:28,876
Yes.

616
00:30:28,899 --> 00:30:32,939
You can refill your water for free!

617
00:30:32,963 --> 00:30:34,963
It's free?

618
00:30:34,986 --> 00:30:37,153
That’s so exciting!

619
00:30:37,176 --> 00:30:40,542
Here’s the water refill station.

620
00:30:40,565 --> 00:30:43,572
Could you show me how to use it?

621
00:30:43,596 --> 00:30:47,596
Place your bottle and press the button.

622
00:30:47,619 --> 00:30:50,869
Is there cold water available?

623
00:30:50,892 --> 00:30:54,226
The blue button is for cold water.

624
00:30:54,249 --> 00:30:57,415
I'll press the blue button.

625
00:30:57,438 --> 00:30:58,917
Yes.

626
00:30:58,941 --> 00:31:01,417
Here comes the water.

627
00:31:01,441 --> 00:31:04,082
That's 500 milliliters.

628
00:31:04,105 --> 00:31:05,872
Thank you.

629
00:31:05,895 --> 00:31:08,986
Don’t forget to close the cap.

630
00:31:09,010 --> 00:31:11,224
This water is delicious!

631
00:31:11,247 --> 00:31:14,080
I'll take a sip.

632
00:31:14,103 --> 00:31:17,080
It's cold and refreshing!

633
00:31:17,103 --> 00:31:20,507
Bringing your own bottle is eco-friendly!

634
00:31:20,531 --> 00:31:24,200
No need to buy plastic bottles.

635
00:31:24,223 --> 00:31:26,857
It's good for the environment.

636
00:31:26,880 --> 00:31:30,530
Are there other places to refill water?

637
00:31:30,553 --> 00:31:33,620
You can check with an app.

638
00:31:33,643 --> 00:31:37,287
What's the name of the app?

639
00:31:37,310 --> 00:31:40,144
It's called 'mymizu'.

640
00:31:40,167 --> 00:31:43,100
I'll install the app.

641
00:31:43,123 --> 00:31:46,323
You'll find plenty of refill spots!

642
00:31:46,346 --> 00:31:50,013
It's hot out, so please be careful.

643
00:31:50,036 --> 00:31:53,836
Could I rest inside the shop for a bit?

644
00:31:53,859 --> 00:31:55,459
Yes.

645
00:31:55,482 --> 00:31:57,215
Here you go.

646
00:31:57,238 --> 00:31:59,112
Please take a seat and rest.

647
00:31:59,136 --> 00:32:02,302
I'll order an iced coffee.

648
00:32:02,325 --> 00:32:03,925
Thank you.

649
00:32:03,948 --> 00:32:07,002
It feels so nice and cool.

650
00:32:07,026 --> 00:32:09,277
Take your time.

651
00:32:09,301 --> 00:32:13,568
The coffee is 450 yen.

652
00:32:13,591 --> 00:32:17,026
Yes, that's 450 yen.

653
00:32:17,050 --> 00:32:19,289
I'll pay by card.

654
00:32:19,312 --> 00:32:21,450
Please tap here to pay.

655
00:32:21,473 --> 00:32:23,492
Payment complete.

656
00:32:23,515 --> 00:32:25,412
Thank you very much.

657
00:32:25,435 --> 00:32:28,802
Thank you for the water refill tips!

658
00:32:28,825 --> 00:32:31,393
I'll be walking now.

659
00:32:31,416 --> 00:32:34,950
Enjoy your trip to Tokyo!

660
00:32:34,973 --> 00:32:36,473
Scene 15: Beat the Heat – Cool Down Essentials for Hot Days

661
00:32:36,473 --> 00:32:38,306
Excuse me.

662
00:32:38,329 --> 00:32:41,896
I'm looking for items to help with the heat.

663
00:32:41,919 --> 00:32:44,362
Right over here.

664
00:32:44,385 --> 00:32:47,585
Do you have a spray to cool down clothes?

665
00:32:47,608 --> 00:32:50,299
Yes, this is the one.

666
00:32:50,322 --> 00:32:53,858
Does it make clothes feel cooler when sprayed?

667
00:32:53,882 --> 00:32:57,049
Yes, it makes your clothes feel cold.

668
00:32:57,072 --> 00:33:00,205
Do you have any wipes to wipe off sweat?

669
00:33:00,228 --> 00:33:03,495
Yes, we have cooling wipes.

670
00:33:03,518 --> 00:33:06,210
I'll take these cooling wipes.

671
00:33:06,233 --> 00:33:09,321
They stay cold for a long time.

672
00:33:09,344 --> 00:33:11,978
Do you have any salt candies?

673
00:33:12,001 --> 00:33:16,134
Yes, we have lemon-flavored salt candies.

674
00:33:16,157 --> 00:33:19,002
You eat them when you sweat, right?

675
00:33:19,026 --> 00:33:21,792
Yes, they're good for you.

676
00:33:21,815 --> 00:33:24,017
I'll buy some drinks too.

677
00:33:24,041 --> 00:33:27,208
The drinks are over there.

678
00:33:27,231 --> 00:33:29,665
I'll take four items in total.

679
00:33:29,688 --> 00:33:31,621
Thank you.

680
00:33:31,644 --> 00:33:33,922
Can I get tax-free on this?

681
00:33:33,946 --> 00:33:38,512
Tax-free applies if your purchase is over 5,500 yen.

682
00:33:38,535 --> 00:33:40,902
May I see your passport?

683
00:33:40,925 --> 00:33:43,569
Here's my passport.

684
00:33:43,592 --> 00:33:46,431
Alright, no tax will be applied.

685
00:33:46,455 --> 00:33:48,688
How much is it in total?

686
00:33:48,711 --> 00:33:52,378
It's 6,000 yen with tax-free.

687
00:33:52,401 --> 00:33:54,968
Can I pay with a card?

688
00:33:54,991 --> 00:33:58,557
Yes, you can pay with a tap.

689
00:33:58,580 --> 00:34:01,180
I'll tap my card.

690
00:34:01,203 --> 00:34:03,337
Okay, that's all set.

691
00:34:03,360 --> 00:34:07,418
Is it okay to open the tax-free bag in Japan?

692
00:34:07,441 --> 00:34:11,057
No, you must not open it in Japan.

693
00:34:11,080 --> 00:34:15,213
Do I need to pay separately for the spray I'll use today?

694
00:34:15,236 --> 00:34:20,125
Yes, please pay for today's items at the regular register.

695
00:34:20,149 --> 00:34:23,483
I'll just buy one spray separately.

696
00:34:23,505 --> 00:34:26,072
That'll be 480 yen.

697
00:34:26,095 --> 00:34:30,554
Here's 500 yen. Here's your 20 yen change.

698
00:34:30,578 --> 00:34:32,461
I'll use it right away.

699
00:34:32,484 --> 00:34:35,339
Stay cool and take care!

700
00:34:35,362 --> 00:34:36,862
Scene 16: Skip the Lines – Smooth Airport Experience with Facial Recognition

701
00:34:36,862 --> 00:34:42,629
Did you see the news about the new airport system?

702
00:34:42,652 --> 00:34:45,422
No, I haven't.

703
00:34:45,446 --> 00:34:47,813
What kind of system is it?

704
00:34:47,836 --> 00:34:52,308
It's called Face Express.

705
00:34:52,331 --> 00:34:57,390
You can board your flight without showing your passport.

706
00:34:57,414 --> 00:35:01,293
You mean I can go through without my passport?

707
00:35:01,316 --> 00:35:03,516
That's amazing!

708
00:35:03,539 --> 00:35:08,187
First, you take a photo of your face with the machine.

709
00:35:08,210 --> 00:35:11,744
It matches your face with your passport.

710
00:35:11,767 --> 00:35:17,367
After taking the photo, checking in your luggage is faster.

711
00:35:17,390 --> 00:35:21,723
No need to take out your passport—so convenient!

712
00:35:21,746 --> 00:35:25,179
The wait time is much shorter.

713
00:35:25,202 --> 00:35:29,216
You can get through the gate faster.

714
00:35:29,240 --> 00:35:32,606
Can I use this at Narita or Haneda Airport?

715
00:35:32,629 --> 00:35:36,829
Yes, you can use it at both Narita and Haneda.

716
00:35:36,852 --> 00:35:39,858
Can anyone use this system?

717
00:35:39,882 --> 00:35:44,449
If you have an e-passport, you can use it!

718
00:35:44,472 --> 00:35:48,838
My passport has an IC chip.

719
00:35:48,861 --> 00:35:52,117
Then you can use it!

720
00:35:52,141 --> 00:35:55,144
Is the facial recognition data secure?

721
00:35:55,167 --> 00:35:58,800
It’s deleted after you board the plane.

722
00:35:58,823 --> 00:36:01,071
Does it disappear right away?

723
00:36:01,095 --> 00:36:03,180
That’s reassuring.

724
00:36:03,203 --> 00:36:05,537
It’s a very secure system.

725
00:36:05,560 --> 00:36:08,626
So I just look at the camera at the gate?

726
00:36:08,649 --> 00:36:12,516
Yes, just look at the camera, and it opens.

727
00:36:12,539 --> 00:36:15,907
No need to dig out your passport.

728
00:36:15,931 --> 00:36:19,141
Such a relief when you have a lot of luggage!

729
00:36:19,164 --> 00:36:23,242
I’d love to try it next time I go back home.

730
00:36:23,266 --> 00:36:27,141
It’s so easy—give it a try!

731
00:36:27,165 --> 00:36:29,854
There’s staff nearby if you need help.

732
00:36:29,877 --> 00:36:33,611
Thanks for sharing the news!

733
00:36:33,634 --> 00:36:36,800
Safe travels!

734
00:36:36,823 --> 00:36:40,057
I’ll take a photo at the airport to show you.

735
00:36:40,080 --> 00:36:42,121
Looking forward to it!

736
00:36:42,144 --> 00:36:44,011
Take care. See you later.

737
00:36:44,034 --> 00:36:45,534
Scene 17: How to Use the Facial Recognition System

738
00:36:45,534 --> 00:36:47,534
Excuse me.

739
00:36:47,557 --> 00:36:51,157
I’d like to use the facial recognition system.

740
00:36:51,180 --> 00:36:52,349
Yes.

741
00:36:52,373 --> 00:36:55,606
You can do it at this machine.

742
00:36:55,629 --> 00:36:59,700
Press the Face Express button.

743
00:36:59,724 --> 00:37:02,214
Pressed it.

744
00:37:02,237 --> 00:37:08,771
Select English on the right side of the screen, then press 'Yes.'

745
00:37:08,794 --> 00:37:11,081
Pressed 'Yes.'

746
00:37:11,104 --> 00:37:15,556
Next, open your passport to the photo page.

747
00:37:15,580 --> 00:37:19,260
Placing the photo page now.

748
00:37:19,283 --> 00:37:21,759
It scanned successfully.

749
00:37:21,783 --> 00:37:25,949
Your name and passport number appear.

750
00:37:25,972 --> 00:37:28,510
Press 'Confirm.'

751
00:37:28,534 --> 00:37:31,134
Pressed 'Confirm.'

752
00:37:31,157 --> 00:37:34,690
Now, look at the camera.

753
00:37:34,713 --> 00:37:38,580
Taking off my hat and mask.

754
00:37:38,603 --> 00:37:42,648
Yes, please remove your hat and mask.

755
00:37:42,671 --> 00:37:46,129
Looking straight at the camera.

756
00:37:46,153 --> 00:37:49,319
The machine will take your photo.

757
00:37:49,342 --> 00:37:50,789
Yes.

758
00:37:50,813 --> 00:37:54,379
It just took the photo!

759
00:37:54,402 --> 00:37:56,887
Facial recognition complete.

760
00:37:56,911 --> 00:38:00,152
Is that all?

761
00:38:00,176 --> 00:38:01,822
Yes.

762
00:38:01,846 --> 00:38:04,379
Your boarding pass will print now.

763
00:38:04,402 --> 00:38:06,569
Here’s the boarding pass.

764
00:38:06,592 --> 00:38:10,759
It has the Face Express logo.

765
00:38:10,782 --> 00:38:13,515
There’s a blue mark on it.

766
00:38:13,538 --> 00:38:18,572
Now you can go through baggage inspection using just your face!

767
00:38:18,596 --> 00:38:23,529
No need to take out your passport—so convenient!

768
00:38:23,552 --> 00:38:27,485
Can I use this machine for my luggage?

769
00:38:27,508 --> 00:38:28,927
Yes.

770
00:38:28,951 --> 00:38:32,963
Yes, you can use that machine over there.

771
00:38:32,986 --> 00:38:35,720
I'm going to check in my luggage.

772
00:38:35,743 --> 00:38:37,623
That was easy.

773
00:38:37,647 --> 00:38:39,144
Thank you.

774
00:38:39,167 --> 00:38:41,767
Have a great trip!

775
00:38:41,790 --> 00:38:43,957
Have a safe trip!

776
00:38:43,980 --> 00:38:45,480
Scene 18: How to Self-Check Your Luggage

777
00:38:45,480 --> 00:38:47,446
Excuse me.

778
00:38:47,469 --> 00:38:51,755
Can I check in my luggage by myself?

779
00:38:51,779 --> 00:38:52,913
Yes.

780
00:38:52,936 --> 00:38:55,869
Please use this machine.

781
00:38:55,892 --> 00:38:59,460
This is my first time self-checking my luggage.

782
00:38:59,484 --> 00:39:01,951
Press the start button.

783
00:39:01,975 --> 00:39:04,341
I pressed the start button.

784
00:39:04,364 --> 00:39:07,164
Please look at the camera above.

785
00:39:07,187 --> 00:39:11,164
I just took a photo of my face.

786
00:39:11,188 --> 00:39:15,121
The camera will recognize your face when you look at it.

787
00:39:15,144 --> 00:39:17,724
My name appeared on the screen.

788
00:39:17,747 --> 00:39:20,759
Place your luggage on the machine.

789
00:39:20,782 --> 00:39:23,449
I'll place it in the center.

790
00:39:23,472 --> 00:39:24,872
Yes.

791
00:39:24,895 --> 00:39:27,497
Please place it sideways.

792
00:39:27,520 --> 00:39:29,753
The weight is displayed.

793
00:39:29,776 --> 00:39:32,230
It's eighteen kilograms.

794
00:39:32,254 --> 00:39:34,029
Is that okay?

795
00:39:34,053 --> 00:39:38,391
Yes, it's fine since the limit is twenty-three kilograms.

796
00:39:38,415 --> 00:39:40,415
That's a relief.

797
00:39:40,438 --> 00:39:43,320
Do you have any dangerous items?

798
00:39:43,343 --> 00:39:46,786
Do you have a laptop or batteries inside?

799
00:39:46,810 --> 00:39:49,843
I have batteries in my backpack.

800
00:39:49,866 --> 00:39:53,550
Batteries cannot be checked in with the machine.

801
00:39:53,574 --> 00:39:55,418
Got it.

802
00:39:55,441 --> 00:39:57,730
I'll carry them myself.

803
00:39:57,754 --> 00:40:00,987
Now, please press 'Yes'.

804
00:40:01,010 --> 00:40:03,943
A long sticker will come out.

805
00:40:03,966 --> 00:40:05,843
The sticker came out.

806
00:40:05,867 --> 00:40:09,733
Please attach the sticker to the handle of your luggage.

807
00:40:09,756 --> 00:40:12,290
I'll attach it to the handle.

808
00:40:12,313 --> 00:40:14,768
You attached it neatly!

809
00:40:14,791 --> 00:40:17,078
What's next?

810
00:40:17,101 --> 00:40:19,901
Please press the 'Finish' button.

811
00:40:19,924 --> 00:40:22,724
I pressed the 'Finish' button.

812
00:40:22,747 --> 00:40:25,814
Your luggage will go inside now.

813
00:40:25,837 --> 00:40:28,104
The luggage went in.

814
00:40:28,126 --> 00:40:30,335
A receipt will come out.

815
00:40:30,359 --> 00:40:32,492
I got the paper.

816
00:40:32,515 --> 00:40:35,163
Please keep it safe.

817
00:40:35,187 --> 00:40:38,154
I'll put it in my passport case.

818
00:40:38,177 --> 00:40:40,344
It only took a minute.

819
00:40:40,367 --> 00:40:44,137
Next, please proceed to the luggage inspection.

820
00:40:44,160 --> 00:40:45,649
Thank you.

821
00:40:45,673 --> 00:41:05,939
Have a nice day!

822
00:41:05,962 --> 00:41:07,462
Scene 19: Facial Recognition Procedure

823
00:41:07,462 --> 00:41:09,229
Excuse me.

824
00:41:09,252 --> 00:41:12,252
Is this where I get my luggage inspected?

825
00:41:12,275 --> 00:41:15,343
Yes, this is the place.

826
00:41:15,367 --> 00:41:18,501
I just took a photo of my face.

827
00:41:18,524 --> 00:41:21,957
Please go through the path on the right.

828
00:41:21,980 --> 00:41:24,247
I'll go to the right.

829
00:41:24,271 --> 00:41:28,604
There's no one here, so you can go right away.

830
00:41:28,627 --> 00:41:31,361
Do I need to show my passport?

831
00:41:31,384 --> 00:41:35,317
No, just look at the camera.

832
00:41:35,340 --> 00:41:38,150
Please stand on the yellow mark.

833
00:41:38,173 --> 00:41:41,540
Looking straight at the camera.

834
00:41:41,563 --> 00:41:44,455
I'll remove your mask and hat now.

835
00:41:44,479 --> 00:41:48,497
Okay, I can see your face clearly.

836
00:41:48,520 --> 00:41:50,361
The door has opened.

837
00:41:50,385 --> 00:41:52,554
Let's go inside.

838
00:41:52,577 --> 00:41:57,211
No need to take out your passport—it's faster this way.

839
00:41:57,234 --> 00:42:00,167
We'll inspect any items you're carrying.

840
00:42:00,190 --> 00:42:03,201
Please place your luggage in the tray.

841
00:42:03,224 --> 00:42:05,957
What should I do with my laptop?

842
00:42:05,980 --> 00:42:09,648
Please take your laptop out of your bag.

843
00:42:09,672 --> 00:42:12,039
Okay, I've taken it out.

844
00:42:12,062 --> 00:42:15,197
Do you have any drinks in there?

845
00:42:15,220 --> 00:42:17,587
I have water.

846
00:42:17,611 --> 00:42:22,891
You can't bring water over 100 milliliters with you.

847
00:42:22,915 --> 00:42:25,166
I'll dispose of it here.

848
00:42:25,190 --> 00:42:28,123
Please use the trash bin over there.

849
00:42:28,146 --> 00:42:31,146
Please remove any thick jackets.

850
00:42:31,169 --> 00:42:33,838
Take out any coins from your pockets too.

851
00:42:33,862 --> 00:42:37,157
I'll put my phone in the tray as well.

852
00:42:37,180 --> 00:42:42,146
Okay. Please remove thick shoes and put on these slippers.

853
00:42:42,169 --> 00:42:44,148
Got it.

854
00:42:44,172 --> 00:42:48,105
Now, please walk through this gate.

855
00:42:48,129 --> 00:42:49,729
Going through.

856
00:42:49,752 --> 00:42:53,595
No alarm sounded—you're good to go.

857
00:42:53,619 --> 00:42:56,790
Please collect your belongings.

858
00:42:56,813 --> 00:42:58,226
Thank you very much.

859
00:42:58,250 --> 00:43:00,703
Proceed to your flight.

860
00:43:00,726 --> 00:43:03,093
Have a nice day!

861
00:43:03,116 --> 00:43:04,616
Scene 20: Passport Inspection Process

862
00:43:04,616 --> 00:43:06,508
Excuse me.

863
00:43:06,531 --> 00:43:09,824
Is this where I get my passport checked?

864
00:43:09,847 --> 00:43:12,847
Yes, this is the place.

865
00:43:12,870 --> 00:43:16,404
Can I use the automated gate?

866
00:43:16,427 --> 00:43:20,870
If you have an e-passport, you can use it.

867
00:43:20,893 --> 00:43:23,826
I'll head to the automated gate then.

868
00:43:23,849 --> 00:43:26,849
Please open your passport to the photo page.

869
00:43:26,872 --> 00:43:29,239
I've opened it.

870
00:43:29,262 --> 00:43:32,870
Place it face-down on the scanner.

871
00:43:32,893 --> 00:43:35,260
Putting my passport on the scanner.

872
00:43:35,283 --> 00:43:38,087
The system has read your passport.

873
00:43:38,110 --> 00:43:42,943
The screen says, 'Look at the camera.'

874
00:43:42,966 --> 00:43:44,400
Yes.

875
00:43:44,423 --> 00:43:48,456
Please remove your hat and glasses, then look at the camera.

876
00:43:48,479 --> 00:43:51,212
I'll take off my glasses.

877
00:43:51,235 --> 00:43:54,202
Verifying your facial recognition.

878
00:43:54,225 --> 00:43:57,706
The gate has opened.

879
00:43:57,729 --> 00:43:59,814
Please go ahead.

880
00:43:59,838 --> 00:44:02,304
I'll take my passport.

881
00:44:02,327 --> 00:44:04,861
Don't forget it!

882
00:44:04,884 --> 00:44:09,050
The automated gate doesn't stamp passports, does it?

883
00:44:09,073 --> 00:44:11,724
I'd love a stamp as a souvenir.

884
00:44:11,747 --> 00:44:14,844
I can stamp it for you!

885
00:44:14,868 --> 00:44:16,913
This way, please.

886
00:44:16,936 --> 00:44:18,709
Yes, please do.

887
00:44:18,733 --> 00:44:21,899
I've stamped your passport.

888
00:44:21,922 --> 00:44:23,489
Thank you.

889
00:44:23,512 --> 00:44:26,120
I did some shopping.

890
00:44:26,143 --> 00:44:29,479
Do you need to show the tax-free receipt?

891
00:44:29,503 --> 00:44:34,070
Your data is already registered, so no need to show it.

892
00:44:34,093 --> 00:44:36,909
The process is so simple, isn't it?

893
00:44:36,932 --> 00:44:40,202
We got through quickly, didn't we?

894
00:44:40,226 --> 00:44:43,260
Which gate do I board the plane from?

895
00:44:43,283 --> 00:44:46,582
Check the right side of your ticket.

896
00:44:46,606 --> 00:44:49,385
It says Gate 65.

897
00:44:49,409 --> 00:44:53,461
Turn left and it's a five-minute walk.

898
00:44:53,484 --> 00:44:56,051
Do we have time to get to the plane?

899
00:44:56,074 --> 00:44:58,686
We still have an hour left.

900
00:44:58,709 --> 00:45:01,309
Feel free to do some shopping at the stores.

901
00:45:01,332 --> 00:45:03,466
I'll pick up some souvenirs.

902
00:45:03,489 --> 00:45:06,061
Have a wonderful trip!

903
00:45:06,084 --> 00:45:08,064
Yes, thank you.

904
00:45:08,088 --> 00:45:10,660
Have a nice day!